#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087567 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "8559e2bf-8b48-5e26-81c6-0db03d93645a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5451" :question/problem "What linear transformation is represented by the matrix\n![](images/03/0394b5d3a371caf95d5e701c0ffb00894eb685e706d8b70af2149057de0b0cb5.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j} \\}$ of the Euclidean plane $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as depicted below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nWe can find the images of $\\{ \\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j} \\}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/b9/b93bb91dae85a3e3b40a8d0ade3d4f420064aaa6926431fa7f664c977bb8fd59.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents the reflection across the $x$-axis."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087568 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/id #uuid "ef17b637-7c4d-5515-99b7-13b1290244f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-5452" :question/problem "A linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ represents a dilation. Given that ![](images/bd/bd6574ee05b60919de656a889f8532e5a512b381eae63f7a65f251a7afe72738.png) and ![](images/be/be73c2a933a6fb99eaa389774a618848bdadd9cafdf0fcd2f6af126b49b87707.png) what is the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}) = \\dfrac{1}{4}\\mathbf{v},$ we conclude that the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k = \\dfrac{1}{4}.$\n\nRemember that the matrix representing a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n![](images/48/4866597a50fbdb530e9275c77f2ca926c932c7cc334635bd05191aaddd510d75.png)\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n![](images/96/962b9458714f9b7f6b17fe2259e140dfabba443d8ecb5b9e2328172ab3f8a1a2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "015f808a-c2bc-507e-8f20-bbd2cb4811ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396000} {:answer/id #uuid "63d77cc9-bcd1-5fdf-b729-52e06ccab36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396001} {:answer/id #uuid "2b02233e-2dae-5a79-9684-11c096b79aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396002} {:answer/id #uuid "90b07ab8-256d-5a91-b9cc-79d3fb993b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{12}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396003} {:answer/id #uuid "c91805f4-1cf7-5369-8fb0-b501bd5870f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $x=12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63d77cc9-bcd1-5fdf-b729-52e06ccab36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396001} :answer-field/id #uuid "853df19f-413a-5dcd-bd31-575962ee5db9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0591c45f-50ff-5065-b712-d7946fc4e140" :question/math-academy-id "q-12043" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=12.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ad4e4e-04cb-51fe-abe1-4e867e431a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=x+\\frac{2}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401139} {:answer/id #uuid "5a15a75a-e128-599b-b3b9-5645e7305697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=\\frac{2}{3}x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401140} {:answer/id #uuid "f0452ac4-63df-52cb-a5ba-4c3d6f3508db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{2}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401141} {:answer/id #uuid "4708c967-b8d8-54c4-ada0-7e3e2fab1f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{3}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401142} {:answer/id #uuid "d94c5e9f-ee52-566e-9640-baf243e6ea0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=\\frac{2}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0452ac4-63df-52cb-a5ba-4c3d6f3508db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{2}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401141} :answer-field/id #uuid "7629eca5-066a-5cf0-88fc-0ed79060b5bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bb92e93-2cdf-508a-a231-165363849a16" :question/math-academy-id "q-159764" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $\\frac{2}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bf9f258-5df6-5ab0-8e36-0e37244aaae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345445} {:answer/id #uuid "3d8dabe7-de84-57ee-a2d1-48c1a8993593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345871} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea2f815-0c82-56b8-ac82-779ec2cd4152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346021} {:answer/id #uuid "c40f1a03-4e74-5291-a60e-58c10941d399" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347045} {:answer/id #uuid "f87386be-70e5-57da-a04b-9715546afa4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ea2f815-0c82-56b8-ac82-779ec2cd4152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346021} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ce04cad-1f03-5a00-a024-317c9a3f8ee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d4333e7-3a3e-56f4-8135-82a56303935f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78253" :question/problem "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-60 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}$ and $T(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-60 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{1}{3}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f349316-377d-5aca-8be0-efe51d753db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393816} {:answer/id #uuid "dedf8d0c-b6a1-59f1-883a-5982d3e19042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{12} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393817} {:answer/id #uuid "a01f94ce-601f-53bf-a5fa-db638dc5b7fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{12} \\\\ \\frac{1}{12} & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393818} {:answer/id #uuid "3adb433f-4c50-534e-ac8e-6a7b14b14742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{12} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393819} {:answer/id #uuid "90d52da3-230b-5e92-b23d-cd1f57b69723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3adb433f-4c50-534e-ac8e-6a7b14b14742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{12} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393819} :answer-field/id #uuid "0042b03d-3295-5843-b9f4-bcbbd57892c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7309edc8-4532-58c0-ac70-deeef25e93b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-78294" :question/problem "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=\\begin{bmatrix}60 \\\\ 144\\end{bmatrix}$ and $T(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix},$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}60 \\\\ 144\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{1}{12}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{1}{12}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{12} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393821 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebd1c492-bc34-536a-93af-528535ac0dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{9} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393823} {:answer/id #uuid "2527ce77-64be-5a89-9267-c574afcbee7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393824} {:answer/id #uuid "83949906-5947-5c67-8c2d-a083cec8ad9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{9} & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393825} {:answer/id #uuid "868da73a-ea9a-5f95-989a-9c024bc284cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{9} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393826} {:answer/id #uuid "f66fdf6a-68cd-54e5-81ef-28e0fbde30f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{9} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f66fdf6a-68cd-54e5-81ef-28e0fbde30f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{9} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393827} :answer-field/id #uuid "0da0ed2f-51d0-5d07-b631-9e8cc54faa32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba67f8b5-b4aa-5dbc-8d3f-1501ac2571d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-78295" :question/problem "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-54 \\\\ 81\\end{bmatrix}$ and $T(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-54 \\\\ 81\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{1}{9}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{1}{9}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{9} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "272ad4ce-b146-5a57-8c5a-5d1e1b3e79ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396717} {:answer/id #uuid "b7fe5771-8880-5a10-a850-ea4baad6b72e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396718} {:answer/id #uuid "c2191dbe-147e-5390-a126-2d6a0061ee2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396719} {:answer/id #uuid "c22c0f50-7b0a-5358-91f1-6489ddb8ffdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396720} {:answer/id #uuid "ace98a54-10d8-5584-91a9-8dc23cfa3eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c22c0f50-7b0a-5358-91f1-6489ddb8ffdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396720} :answer-field/id #uuid "47512c4c-4d28-5025-9b41-fddc19cb1574" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a51c70cd-319b-5de1-a71f-816af37c3370" :question/math-academy-id "q-78302" :question/problem "Which of the following represents a reflection in the line $y=-x?$" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is $T=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/4a/4a83673a409fd2e5d33b0b5f743f57af08cfb27c38e312a636179102c2172b04.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348074 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4330aa67-8eca-534c-a9e9-91a37ada11b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $x=17$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345930} {:answer/id #uuid "551607ae-79d2-5c83-af3d-a8635eff305f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{17}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346072} {:answer/id #uuid "65d47725-4eb6-598c-b932-230b8b362a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346239} {:answer/id #uuid "78f8d6ef-022c-5f56-9e15-fc6e37365741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346409} {:answer/id #uuid "cacbfb3c-c88b-5545-93e1-cb25164a4ea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $17$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cacbfb3c-c88b-5545-93e1-cb25164a4ea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $17$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347121} :answer-field/id #uuid "526ad53a-59d3-5db8-9e7d-1c337e0505d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4db462f3-5435-5b8e-8538-abab7a997273" :question/math-academy-id "q-78337" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 17\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=17.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $17.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fe2e6e8-335c-58be-b255-c60fa43a41f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396192} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa33fd0-bc88-5221-b0ce-b4b35cc3e471" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396193} {:answer/id #uuid "99f4a2a9-46a7-591a-b8d7-dd58887c39ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396194} {:answer/id #uuid "7810d358-12eb-5db3-8061-1d557a816ce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=-x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396195} {:answer/id #uuid "84c9888e-01f7-56a1-a9cc-589307e77959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7810d358-12eb-5db3-8061-1d557a816ce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=-x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396195} :answer-field/id #uuid "4259dafc-1a37-55ff-aa39-09cc98e980bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e53a5dab-4c76-5167-b8bb-303aab059a57" :question/math-academy-id "q-8060" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](images/9e/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we compute the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](images/4a/4a83673a409fd2e5d33b0b5f743f57af08cfb27c38e312a636179102c2172b04.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a reflection in the line $y=-x.$"}]}
